, 5)\n  emit_br(b, 0)\n  emit_end(b)\n  emit_end(b)\n  // return tag(p)\n  emit_local_get(b, 5)\n  if enable_rc {\n    emit_i64_const(b, 1)\n    emit_i64_shl(b)\n  }\n  b\n}\n\n// simd_scan_alnum(buf: Bytes, pos: Int, len: Int) -> Int\n// Returns the smallest index i in [pos, len) such that buf[i] is NOT an\n// identifier byte ([A-Za-z0-9_]); returns len if every byte in the range is an\n// identifier byte. Used to scan to the end of an identifier/number run. A SIMD\n// fast path skips whole 16-byte chunks that are entirely identifier bytes; a\n// scalar tail handles the final partial chunk and the chunk that first contains\n// a non-identifier byte. Range membership uses the wrap-subtract trick\n// (x - lo) <=u (hi - lo). v128 stays on the operand stack (no v128 local).\n//   locals: i32 { 3: addr } ; i64 { 4: p, 5: n, 6: byte }\nexport fn gen_simd_scan_alnum_body(enable_rc: Bool, is_string: Bool) -> Bytes {\n  let b = bytebuf_new()\n  // addr = pointer to the byte payload. Bytes: the payload pointer lives at\n  // obj+8. String: the value packs (ptr|len) with char data at (value >> 32).\n  emit_local_get(b, 0)\n  if is_string {\n    emit_i64_const(b, 32)\n    emit_i64_shr_s(b)\n    emit_i32_wrap_i64(b)\n  } else {\n    emit_i32_wrap_i64(b)\n    emit_i32_load(b, 2, 8)\n  }\n  emit_local_set(b, 3)\n  // p = untag(pos)\n  emit_local_get(b, 1)\n  if enable_rc {\n    emit_i64_const(b, 1)\n    emit_i64_shr_s(b)\n  }\n  emit_local_set(b, 4)\n  // n = untag(len)\n  emit_local_get(b, 2)\n  if enable_rc {\n    emit_i64_const(b, 1)\n    emit_i64_shr_s(b)\n  }\n  emit_local_set(b, 5)\n  // --- SIMD fast path: skip 16-byte chunks that are entirely identifier bytes ---\n  emit_block_void(b)\n  emit_loop_void(b)\n  // if p + 16 > n: leave the fast path\n  emit_local_get(b, 4)\n  emit_i64_const(b, 16)\n  emit_i64_add(b)\n  emit_local_get(b, 5)\n  emit_i64_gt_s(b)\n  emit_br_if(b, 1)\n  // digit: (x - 0x30) <=u 9\n  emit_local_get(b, 3)\n  emit_local_get(b, 4)\n  emit_i32_wrap_i64